course: dictionary
lesson: 11510
title: Airflow: moving air
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Airflow is the movement of air from one place to another. You cannot always see it, but you can feel it on your face when a window is open or a fan is on. Air moves because it flows from one place to another.
explain: «Open the window to let in some fresh airflow.» The words fresh and let in are clues. Fresh air is clean air, and letting it in means air is moving into the room, so airflow must be air moving.
explain: «Please do not block the airflow around the heater.» Block means stop or get in the way. Blocking the airflow means putting something in front of the heater so air cannot move around it. Good airflow keeps machines cool and rooms safe.
fact: Airflow means the movement of air from one place to another.
fact: Airflow can move through a room, through a machine or around a wing.
fact: Airflow around a plane wing helps give the plane lift, so it can fly.
fact: Good airflow cools computers and keeps rooms fresh.
fact: Good airflow, or ventilation, stops fumes from building up in a room.
exercise: «Open the window to let in some fresh airflow.» What does airflow mean? | A type of cold drink | A loud noise made by a fan | *The movement of air from one place to another | A pile of dust on the floor
exercise: «Please do not block the airflow around the heater.» What should you not do? | Open the window to let in fresh air | *Put something in front that stops air moving | Move the heater to a different room | Switch the heater off and on again
exercise: «The fan gives good airflow, so the computer stays cool.» Copy the word that names moving air. | computer | fan | *airflow | cool
test: «Good airflow stops fumes building up in a room.» What does good airflow do? | It makes the room colder | *It lets fumes escape, keeping the air safe | It makes fumes louder | It adds more fumes to the room
test: Ben says the wing needs airflow to lift the plane. What is the airflow in that sentence? | A heavy, still block of air | Fuel burning inside the engine | *Moving air flowing over the wing | A wing made of paper
exam: Which best explains airflow? | A bright light on a desk | *The movement of air from one place to another | A sweet smell in the kitchen | A sound made by a bird
